  "notes": "A hydrophone recording: no beat, no key, a sea-noise bed. Low moans (C♯4–G4: 0:02, 0:09, 0:16, 0:22, 0:28) alternate with high whistles (A♯5–D6: 0:04, 0:12, 0:19, 0:25); from 0:31.7 the calls turn into rising whoops, at 0:42.8 comes the deepest, longest call (the strongest change in the pack), then sparser calls fade out. The melody ribbon traces each call's glide; no pulse anywhere. The biggest accent goes to the deep call, not P1 (a whistle-and-moan overlap at 0:10.6), because it is the moment the song changes.",
